   109	// Surface patch wire types (OCEAN-178)
   110	//
   111	// Self-contained mirror of `ocean-agent-sdk::surface` (GPUI Masterbuild Slice 1)
   112	// so this WASM crate can deserialize the EXACT JSON the daemon streams on a
   113	// `surface_patch` SSE frame — without taking a build dependency on the ocean-os
   114	// workspace (this crate already mirrors every other daemon wire type the same
   115	// way: `ToolCallSummary`, `ToolResult`, etc.). The GPUI shell carries the same
   116	// mirror in `ocean-gui/src/shell/canvas/patch.rs`; the wire contract is fixed in
   117	// `ocean-os/crates/ocean-agent-sdk/src/lib.rs`.
   118	//
   119	// Wire-contract notes (must match the SDK or patches silently route to `Other`):
   120	// - Ids are `serde(transparent)` over `String` — on the wire a `ComponentId` is
   121	//   just `"brief-1"`.
   122	// - `SurfacePatch` is internally tagged on `"op"`, `snake_case`.
   123	// - `SurfacePatchEnvelope.session_id` is carried as a plain `String` here
   124	//   (this crate's convention); the SDK uses a `serde(transparent)` uuid newtype,
   125	//   so the JSON is byte-identical.
