1526	/// When the daemon runs with permission-gating on, a mutating tool call
1527	/// (write / edit / bash) BLOCKS until the operator posts a decision. The daemon
1528	/// emits a `permission_request` on the control stream; `Daemon` collects them in
1529	/// `pending_permissions`. This renders one prominent card per pending request —
1530	/// stacked, oldest first — each with Approve / Deny. Clicking POSTs the decision
1531	/// and clears the card; a decision made elsewhere (e.g. the TUI) clears it via
1532	/// the `permission_decision` frame. A pending request blocks the turn, so the
1533	/// stack is fixed at the bottom of the viewport above the composer and can't be
1534	/// scrolled away.
1535	#[component]
